{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume","lean:module:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_leading_unreachable_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_leading_unreachable_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L259-L270","doc":"**Leading-order unreachability.** If a target `S` exceeds the `Re`-capped\nleading bound `κ·r²`, then NO `u` with real part `r` realizes it at leading\norder: `(V₄₁ u).im = S` is impossible. Instantiated at `r = ln q₀`,\n`S = S_μ`: the muon leak (`= 2.054 × κ(ln q₀)²`) is unreachable for any real\nspin — the magnitude sub-obstruction, orthogonal to the (spin-driven) sign\nflip. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_le_cuspModulus_reSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_le_cuspModulus_reSq","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L249-L257","doc":"**Leading-form upper bound.** `Im 𝔙₄₁(u) ≤ κ·(Re u)²` for every `u`, since the\nimaginary (spin) part only subtracts (`κ·Im²u ≥ 0`). The spin part can flip\nthe sign but never lift the magnitude above the pure-boost value `κ·Re²u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.f3_re_linear_same_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.f3_re_linear_same_sign","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L209-L226","doc":"**F3 cannot sign-flip (the #3773 survivor, refuted against the corrected\nform).** For the F3 family `u = ⟨k·d, c₀⟩` — real part linear-through-zero at\nq* (value `k·d`, `d = q−q*`), imaginary part the anchor-constant `c₀` — as\nlong as the linear excursion stays below the constant, `(k·d)² < c₀²`, the CS\npart is NEGATIVE. Hence at two anchors both with `(k·dᵢ)² < c₀²` the sign is\nthe SAME (both negative): F3 keeps both on the same side of the diagonal and\ncannot reproduce the sign flip. (The mirror sub-case, `Re = a₀`\nconst and `Im = k·d`, is `imV₄₁_pos_iff` with the roles swapped — both\npositive.) This lemma is the small-excursion building block; the fully\nrobust F3 refutation (not assuming `(k·dᵢ)²<c₀²`, but respecting the pinned\nproduct-slope) is the `c₀`-incompatibility argument (`c₀ < c_mu* ≈ 0.0748`\nAND `c₀ > c_pr* ≈ 0.1509` simultaneously — impossible) in\n`sdeformed_channel_signflip_probe.py` + the 2026-07-26 audit; the conclusion\n(F3 cannot reproduce the measured μ>0>p flip) is the same. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.signflip_forces_diagonal_cross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.signflip_forces_diagonal_cross","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L199-L207","doc":"**The sign flip forces a diagonal crossing (T2 invariant).** If the CS part\nis positive at one substrate point and negative at another, then `u` lies in\nOPPOSITE regions relative to the diagonal `|Re u| = |Im u|`: `|Im u₁| < |Re u₁|`\nbut `|Re u₂| < |Im u₂|`. So any `u(q₀)` realizing the measured flip\n`S(muon) > 0 > S(proton)` must cross that diagonal between the anchors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_zero_on_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_zero_on_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L193-L197","doc":"**Im 𝔙₄₁ vanishes on the diagonal** `|Re u| = |Im u|` (i.e. `Re²u = Im²u`),\nnot on the axes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_neg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_neg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L183-L191","doc":"`Im 𝔙₄₁(u) < 0 ↔ |Re u| < |Im u|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L171-L181","doc":"`Im 𝔙₄₁(u) > 0 ↔ |Im u| < |Re u|` (strictly, `u.im² < u.re²`). Sign of the CS\npart = sign of `Re²u − Im²u`, since `κ > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.nzPoly₄₁_no_u3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.nzPoly₄₁_no_u3","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L154-L159","doc":"**No u³ rung for the concrete leading form** (via the proved\n`NeumannZagierParity.no_cubic_rung`): the classical potential's cubic\ncoefficient vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.instNeumannZagierEvenPotentialReal_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.instNeumannZagierEvenPotentialReal_folio","kind":"instance","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L146-L152","doc":"The concrete leading potential instantiates the NZ even-potential class —\nthe parity hypothesis is genuinely satisfied (not fabricated: `Φ₄₁` IS even).\nThis is the §3b-cond parity class of `NeumannZagierParity`, NOT the keystone\nconjecture; no `SDeformedVolumeChannel` instance is produced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.nzPoly₄₁_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.nzPoly₄₁_even","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L143-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.nzPoly₄₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.nzPoly₄₁","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L136-L141","doc":"The classical (Vol-axis) potential of the leading form as a polynomial,\n`Φ₄₁ = Vol(4₁)·1 + κ·X²` — even, and hence with NO cubic (u³) rung by the\nproved `NeumannZagierParity.no_cubic_rung`. This ties the concrete `V₄₁` to\nthe corpus parity prune. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.imV₄₁","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L122-L134","doc":"**Im 𝔙₄₁ is a harmonic quadratic form.** `Im 𝔙₄₁(u) = (√3/4)·(Re²u − Im²u)`\n— the Chern–Simons part is `κ·Re(u²)`; it vanishes on the DIAGONALS\n`|Re u| = |Im u|`, NOT on the coordinate axes. (Contrast the heuristic\n`√3·Re u·Im u` of the earlier gluing probe, which corresponds to a REAL `a₂`\nand is REFUTED by `τ = −i√3`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_even","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L116-L120","doc":"**Neumann–Zagier evenness.** `𝔙₄₁(−u) = 𝔙₄₁(u)` — the deformed complex\nvolume is even in the meridian deformation (NZ: the longitude `v(u)` is odd,\nso the potential is even; `QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_zero_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_zero_im","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L113-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_zero_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_zero_re","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L104-L111","doc":"**Complete-structure value on the Vol axis (EXACT).** `Re 𝔙₄₁(0) = 2·Cl₂(π/3)`\n— the figure-eight hyperbolic volume, with `Im 𝔙₄₁(0) = 0` (CS = 0,\namphichiral). No residual: `a₂` purely imaginary makes the u=0 real part\nexactly the complete-structure volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L100-L102","doc":"𝔙₄₁(0) = Vol(4₁). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L95-L98","doc":"**The figure-eight deformed complex volume, leading Neumann–Zagier form.**\n`𝔙₄₁(u) = Vol(4₁) + i·(√3/4)·u²`, `Vol(4₁) = 2·Cl₂(π/3)`. This concrete\n`ℂ → ℂ` realizes the abstract `SDeformedVolumeChannel.V` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.a₂_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.a₂_im","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.a₂_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.a₂_re","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.a₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.a₂","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L87-L90","doc":"The leading complex-volume coefficient `a₂ = i·(√3/4)` — PURELY IMAGINARY\n(real part 0), the algebraic fingerprint of the ℚ(√−3) cusp modulus\n`τ = −i√3`. This is why `Im 𝔙₄₁` is a harmonic quadratic form in `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.cuspModulus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.cuspModulus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.cuspModulus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.cuspModulus","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightComplexVolume.lean#L77-L81","doc":"The figure-eight cusp modulus `κ = √3/4 = |a₂|` — the magnitude of the\n(purely imaginary) leading Neumann–Zagier complex-volume coefficient.\n`√3/2 = sin(π/3) = Im(e^{iπ/3})` is the cusp shape's imaginary part; the\nfactor `1/2` is the NZ potential normalisation. Geometric datum, not fitted. ","signatureChunk":0}]}